<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Corn rises, soy steady to lower.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Corn rises, soy steady to lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>FOB Gulf corn basis values rose in most positions on Tuesday while soybean positions were steady to lower.</p>
<p>Dealers noted slow movement. &quot;Farmers are holding on to whatever they have. There is not much supply and not much in the pipeline,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>In export news, the Taichung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association bought two 54,000-tonne shipments of U.S. soybeans at a tender on Tuesday. Both shipments were bought from Continental on a cost-and-freight basis.  </p>
